Found by the 0.500 pre-release audit (ticket #39), verified independently: each of the four subs exists, none has an =method or =attr block, so the L<> link resolves to nothing and renders as a dead link on metacpan.

- lib/App/karr/Git.pm:83     L</push_rejections>  -- sub at Git.pm:804
- lib/App/karr/Task.pm:327   L</to_frontmatter>   -- sub at Task.pm:289
- lib/App/karr/Config.pm:102 L</statuses>         -- sub at Config.pm:65
- lib/App/karr/Config.pm:669 L</default_config>   -- sub at Config.pm:552

Note t/author-pod-syntax.t does NOT catch these: it checks POD syntax, not cross-reference resolution, and passes 52/52 against the built tree. podchecker against the WOVEN build tree is what surfaced them -- against the source tree its output is drowned in "Unknown directive: =attr/=method/=func" noise, since those are Author::GETTY PodWeaver directives podchecker does not know.

Fix by writing the four missing blocks in the [@Author::GETTY] convention (inline =method/=attr after the sub), not by deleting the links -- the links are in prose that wants to point somewhere.

Wider context, deliberately NOT part of this ticket: the audit also counted 215 public subs/attributes without a matching =method/=attr block, against 138 in the released 0.402 -- roughly 77 more went undocumented this cycle, concentrated in App::karr::Git (including the new is_tracked_under, delete_ref_cas, save_task_ref_cas, board-id refs) and App::karr::Config. That matches the existing convention in this dist (these modules lean on DESCRIPTION/SYNOPSIS rather than exhaustive per-method POD) and is not a regression, but Git.pm grew a lot of public surface this release and deserves its own pass.
